1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married (1) to the country chamberlain (landskamreren) in  Umeå Lars Torsell, who died 1723. Married (2) to the assessor (assessorn) in Umeå, Peter Bursell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her death record shows she was born 1683-03-22 in Stockholm to Henrik Bröms and Elsa Radsack. Her first husband Lars Torsell died 1723-11-16, and her second husband was an assessor. She died 1723-03-20. Died at age 78 years, 50 we
2 CONC eks (so born about Apr 1763). See transcript of death record.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Death and burial record, Umeå landsförsamling (AC) C:3.50 (1756-1782) (AID: v139889.b67.s50, NAD SE/HLA/1010219/C/3 bildid: A0012915_00068), https://www.arkivdigital.se/aid/show/v139889.b67.s50 or https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvi
2 CONC sning/A0012915_00068
2 CONT Household Exam, Västra Backen, Umeå landsförsamling (AC) AI:6.251  (1757-1767) (AID: v139803.b255.s251, NAD: SE/HLA/1010219)
2 CONT Marriage record to Anna Bröms, Maria Magdalena (AB) EI:1.292, 1725-04-06 (1706-1729) (AID: v88260.b150.s293, NAD: SE/SSA/0012), https://www.arkivdigital.se/aid/show/v88260.b150.s293
2 CONT Örnberg's "Svenska Ättertal," 12 p. 133, for the Norrköping family Bröms
2 CONT Table 12, at https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bröms_från_Norrköping or http://www.mattiasloman.se/broms.html
2 CONT Kråken 13 person 158372 gives sources as "HFL, VR" for birth and "CL" for death; household exam: Umeå/Västra Backen, AI:6,9-10.251 (1757-1761), widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT • Anna Bröms, född 1683, † änka 1761. Gift 1:o 1699 med landskamreren i Umeå Lars Torsell, † 1723. 2:o 1725 med assessorn i Umeå Peter Bursell.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Death and burial record translation:
2 CONT "1762 March 20
2 CONT Assessor’s wife Anna Bröms: born on 22 March 1683. Father: Merchant in Stockholm, Mr.
2 CONT Hendrick Bröms. Mother: Mrs. Elsa Radsack in Stockholm, where she also grew up and on 10 
2 CONT May 1700 married the later Landskamreren [member of the provincial council] here in 
2 CONT Västerbotten, Mr. Lars Torsell. The marriage lasted for 23 1/3 years of happy cohabitation and 
2 CONT was blessed by God with five daughters, all of whom were well provided for.
2 CONT In 1714, she was forced to leave most of her property in the hands of the enemy.[1] She then spent 
2 CONT most of her time in Stockholm. On 16 November 1723, Mr Torsell passed away. On 6 April 1725, 
2 CONT she married Mr. Peter Bursell, the appointed assessor and secretary of the province here in 
2 CONT Umeå. She had only one son with him during their 29 years[2] of marriage, who died in his prime, 
2 CONT not long after his father. The father died on 11 December 1757 and the son on 26 February 1758. 
2 CONT She was gifted with a steady mind, as always.
2 CONT Died 78 [years,] 50 [weeks.]"
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [1] Umeå was burned down by the Russians in 1714.
2 CONT [2] Anna married Bursell in 1725, and he died in 1757. That makes it 32 years, not 29!
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcription:
2 CONT 1762 Mars 5
2 CONT Fru Adsessorskan Anna Bröms: född 1683. D[en]: 22. Martii. Fadren: Handelsmannen i Stockholm H[er]r Hendrick Bröms. Modren fr[u] Elsa Radsack i Stockholm, ther hon också upföddes, samt år 1700 d[en]: 10. Maii ingick
2 CONT äktenskap med sedermera Lands Camreraren här i Vesterbot[te]n
2 CONT Hr Lars Torsell. Hwilket äkenskap Gud under 23 1/3 års liuf sammanlefnad välsignat med 5. st[ycken]. döttrar, som alla blifvit wäl försedda.
2 CONT År 1714 måste hon lemna sin mesta egendom i fiendens händer1
2 CONT . Vistades sedan merendels i Stockholm. 1723 d[en]: 16. Now[em]bris afsomnade Herr Camereraren Torsell. År 1725 d[en]: 6. April[is] inträdde hon äktenskap
2 CONT med h[er]r förordnade Lands Secreteraren här i Umeh förordnade assessoen Peter
2 CONT Bursell. Haft med honom under 29 års2 sammanlefnad allenast 1 son: hwilken i sina bästa år ej långt efter Fadren afsomnade. Fadren dödde d[en]: 11. Dec[embris]: 1757 Och
2 CONT sonen d[en]. 26. Febr[uaris]: 1758. Var begåfvad med ett stadigt sinne som alltid.
2 CONT [Död] 78 [år,] 50 [vecka.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death and burial record, Umeå landsförsamling (AC) C:3.50 (1756-1782) (AID: v139889.b67.s50, NAD SE/HLA/1010219/C/3 bildid: A0012915_00068), https://www.arkivdigital.se/aid/show/v139889.b67.s50 or https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvi
2 CONC sning/A0012915_00068
